- Have the [proper client tools installed on your local system](../../helpers/client-setup/README.md) to use this guide.

- Checkout the llm-d repo:

{% step tags="ci=skip" %}
export BRANCH=main # branch, tag, or commit hash
git clone https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d.git && cd llm-d && git checkout ${BRANCH}
{% endstep %}

- Set your configuration — the exports below are generated from your picks
  above (plus this guide's constants), and every later step consumes them as
  plain environment variables:

{{ configure_step() }}

> [!NOTE]
> `HF_TOKEN` must be a [valid HuggingFace token](../../helpers/hf-token.md);
> replace `HF_TOKEN_PLACEHOLDER` with your real token.

- Source the common guide environment variables:

{% step %}
export REPO_ROOT=$(realpath $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel))
source ${REPO_ROOT}/guides/env.sh
{% endstep %}

> [!NOTE]
> Some environment variables are common amongst guides; inspect the file
> sourced above so the rest of the guide makes sense.

- Install the Gateway API Inference Extension CRDs:

{% step tags="dry-run=skip" %}
kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api-inference-extension/releases/download/${GAIE_VERSION}/v1-manifests.yaml
{% endstep %}
{% step tags="e2e=skip", hide=true %}
curl -sfL https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api-inference-extension/releases/download/${GAIE_VERSION}/v1-manifests.yaml -o /dev/null
{% endstep %}

- Create a target namespace for the installation:

{% step tags="dry-run=skip" %}
kubectl create namespace ${NAMESPACE} --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
{% endstep %}
{% step tags="e2e=skip", hide=true %}
kubectl create namespace ${NAMESPACE} --dry-run=client -o yaml > /dev/null
{% endstep %}

- [Create the `llm-d-hf-token` secret in your target namespace with the key `HF_TOKEN` matching a valid HuggingFace token](../../helpers/hf-token.md) to pull models:

{% step tags="ci=skip" %}
kubectl create secret generic llm-d-hf-token \
  --from-literal="HF_TOKEN=${HF_TOKEN}" \
  --namespace "${NAMESPACE}" \
  --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
{% endstep %}
